#. Tag: title
#: configuration.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kexi;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes how you can configure &kexi; to suit your own needs "
"and preferences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuration.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "Window Layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kexi; provides a <firstterm>Multiple Document Interface</firstterm> (MDI). "
"This means that you can have several database objects (such as tables, "
"queries, forms and scripts) open at the same time and in the same &kexi; "
"main window. Each database object is shown in a <firstterm>child window</"
"firstterm> within the main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a choice of two MDI modes available, allowing a choice of how child "
"windows are managed and displayed. The two modes are: <itemizedlist> "
"<listitem><para><guisubmenu>IDEAl Mode</guisubmenu>; and</para></listitem> "
"<listitem><para><guisubmenu>Childframe Mode</guisubmenu>.</para></listitem> "
"</itemizedlist> These modes are described in the following two sections. You "
"can change the MDI mode from the <guisubmenu>MDI Mode</guisubmenu> sub-menu "
"under the <guimenu>Window</guimenu> menu. Note that changing the MDI mode "
"requires &kexi; to be restarted before the new mode takes effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuration.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid "IDEAl mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"IDEAl mode is the default MDI mode, and may be familiar from other &kde; "
"applications. In this mode, a single child window is shown maximized within "
"the &kexi; main window at once. A tab bar, containing one tab for each child "
"window, allows other child windows to be viewed by simply clicking on the "
"relevant tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuration.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Childframe mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In Childframe mode, child windows are displayed in the main &kexi; window, "
"but need not be maximized within it. In order to use Childframe mode, you "
"need to select <action> <guimenu>Window</guimenu>, <guisubmenu>MDI Mode</"
"guisubmenu>, <guimenuitem>Childframe Mode</guimenuitem> </action> from the "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each child window has a title bar with buttons for maximizing, minimizing "
"and closing it. They can also be moved and resized within the main window in "
"the normal way (for example, they can be moved by clicking and dragging the "
"title bar)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The buttons behave as follows: the right-most button closes the child "
"window. The button on its left maximizes the child window - note this causes "
"the buttons to move to the top right of the main window, above the "
"<guilabel>Properties editor</guilabel> if it is open. The next button to the "
"left toggles the child window between minimized and restored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The left-most button detaches, or <firstterm>undocks</firstterm>, the child "
"window, allowing it to be moved out of the main window. For more information "
"on docking and undocking windows, see the next section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuration.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Docking and Undocking Windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, the <guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Properties Editor</guilabel> panels are displayed as part of the "
"main &kexi; window. It is possible to <firstterm>undock</firstterm> each "
"panel, so that it is displayed in a separate window. Once undocked, it is "
"possible to <firstterm>dock</firstterm> the panel so it appears back in the "
"main window again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In <link linkend=\"window-layout-childframe\">Childframe mode</link>, it is "
"also possible to undock child windows. For example, a child window showing a "
"database table could be undocked, allowing the child window showing the "
"table to be maximized on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "It can be useful to undock a window when using:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "a small screen;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "large tables, queries or forms; and/or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "more than one monitor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuration.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Docking and undocking side panels"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Project Navigator</guilabel> and <guilabel>Properties Editor</"
"guilabel> side panels may be undocked by either:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "double-clicking on the 'grip' bar at the top of the panel; or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:149 configuration.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "clicking once on the arrow at the top of the panel, next to the cross."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once undocked, panel windows may be docked into the main window again "
"similarly to undocking:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "double-clicking on the 'grip' bar at the top of the window; or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: configuration.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Docking and undocking child windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Child windows may be docked and undocked in <link linkend=\"window-layout-"
"childframe\">Childframe mode</link> only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "In Childframe mode, child windows may be undocked by:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"right-clicking in the tab bar, on the tab corresponding to the window to be "
"undocked, and selecting <guilabel>Undock</guilabel>; or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"right-clicking on the title bar of the child window, and selecting "
"<guilabel>Undock</guilabel>; or"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if the child window is <emphasis>not</emphasis> maximized, clicking the "
"arrow in the top right corner of the child window (next to the minimize, "
"maximize and close buttons for that child window);"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if the child window is maximized, clicking the arrow to the right of the "
"menu bar (next to the minimize, restore and close buttons for that child "
"window)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: configuration.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To dock a child window, right-clicking in the tab bar, on the tab "
"corresponding to the window to be docked, and select <guilabel>Dock</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""
